{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ModelsOfQous.WittVectorLift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ModelsOfQous.WittVectorLift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.witt_ring_uniformizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.witt_ring_uniformizer","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L106-L116","doc":"W(𝔽_p) ≅ ℤ_p: the Witt vector ring of a finite field of\nprime order is isomorphic to the p-adic integers. The key\nproperty is that W(𝔽_p) is the unique complete DVR with\nresidue field 𝔽_p and uniformizer p.\n\nWe verify the basic arithmetic: p^2 > p for any prime p. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.relevant_primes_ge_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.relevant_primes_ge_five","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L99-L104","doc":"For the QOU application, the relevant primes are p ≥ 5\n(so that 30 = 2 · 3 · 5 is invertible mod p for p > 5,\nor p = 5 which divides 30 but is handled separately). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.witt_lift_descartes_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.witt_lift_descartes_dim","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L89-L97","doc":"The Witt vector lift is compatible with the Descartes condition:\nwhen the Euler characteristic is -6, the genus is 4, and the\nformal group dimension is 2g = 8.\n\nThis connects the Witt lift to the global Descartes structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.dist_algebra_generators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.dist_algebra_generators","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L79-L87","doc":"The distribution algebra Dist(Ĝ) as a ℤ_p-module has rank\ndetermined by the height and the Lie dimension.\n\nFor a 1-dimensional formal group of height h, Dist(Ĝ) is\na free ℤ_p-module of countable rank with a PBW-type basis\nindexed by multi-indices of length lieDim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.reduction_preserves_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.reduction_preserves_dim","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L67-L77","doc":"The reduction mod p recovers the original formal group:\nĜ ⊗_{W(𝔽_p)} 𝔽_p ≅ H.\n\nAt the level of Lie algebras, this means\nLie(Ĝ) ⊗_{ℤ_p} 𝔽_p ≅ Lie(H).\n\nWe verify the dimensional identity: the Lie algebra dimension\nis preserved by reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.witt_char_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.witt_char_zero","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L57-L65","doc":"The Witt vector ring W(𝔽_p) has characteristic zero (it is ℤ_p,\nwhich is a domain of characteristic 0). The reduction map\nW(𝔽_p) → 𝔽_p has kernel (p).\n\nWe verify the fundamental identity: for any prime p,\np ≠ 0 in ℤ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WittVectorLift.p_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WittVectorLift.p_pos","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The Witt vector ring W(𝔽_p) is p-adically complete:\nencoded as the property that p > 0 in the base. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WittVectorLift.lie_dim_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WittVectorLift.lie_dim_pos","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Lie dimension is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WittVectorLift.lieDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WittVectorLift.lieDim","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Dimension of the Lie algebra Lie(H). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WittVectorLift.height_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WittVectorLift.height_pos","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Height is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WittVectorLift.height","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WittVectorLift.height","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The height of the formal group (determines isogeny class over 𝔽̄_p). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WittVectorLift.p_prime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WittVectorLift.p_prime","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L44-L44","doc":"p is prime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WittVectorLift.p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WittVectorLift.p","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The prime p (residue characteristic of 𝔽_p). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WittVectorLift.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WittVectorLift.mk","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WittVectorLift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WittVectorLift","kind":"structure","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.lean#L29-L55","doc":"**Witt vector lift**: the formal group Ĝ over W(𝔽_p) ≅ ℤ_p obtained\nfrom a commutative formal group H/𝔽_p via skew-Poisson integration.\n\nThe key data consists of:\n- A prime p (the residue characteristic)\n- The height of the formal group\n- The dimension of the Lie algebra Lie(H)\n- The deformation parameter from the skew-Poisson structure\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:witt-vector-lift}`\nRef: [hazewinkel1978] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-35190-6 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:witt-vector-lift","label":"def:witt-vector-lift","md":"quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lift.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}